The diff shows the new call is placed after the closing brace of the cache-miss block:

```ts
if (...) {
  const data = await this.fetchAvailability(parsedArgs);
  await this.setAvailabilityInCache(parsedArgs, data);
}
// Update SelectedCalendar.updatedAt...
await SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId(this.credential.id, {});
```

So it will execute on every `getAvailability` invocation, including cache hits, adding an extra DB write on a hot path. This is a concrete, diff-grounded performance/architecture concern rather than a directly verifiable functional correctness break (the finding doesn’t claim a runtime error).
